                <pb facs="1228" n="1212" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg1212"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>New York, beginning July 8, sent several reports to the Department concerning the
                    armistice negotiations between Israel and Syria. The report of July 8 stated
                    that there had been general agreement on the <pb facs="1229" n="1213"
                        xml:id="pg1213"/> draft of an armistice and that some demarcation of
                    armistice lines had been achieved (telegram 811, 501.BB Palestine/7—849).</p>
                <p>Disagreements were encountered subsequently, particularly on the location and
                    possible modification of the “certified truce line,” which had been established
                    on July 18, 1948, after the second truce (telegrams 815, 818, and 819 from New
                    York, all dated July 11, 501.BB Palestine/7–1149).</p>
            </div>
        </body>
